% references.bib -- every source in docs/literature/READING_LIST.md
%
% 183 sources, checked 21 October 2026, and checked again the same day. Two rows of the list are several
% datasets each, so they have one entry per package here: D27 (four EPA test
% data packages, D27a-D27d) and D28 (three EPA ALPHA map packages, D28a-D28c).
%
% Import into Zotero: File > Import..., choose this file, keep "Place imported
% collections and items into new collection" ticked. The file is UTF-8.
%
% Every entry carries:
%   keywords  the list id, MUST or SHOULD, the access route (FREE, SDL,
%             SDL-UNCONFIRMED, BUY) and the topic number. Zotero turns them
%             into tags, so you can filter, for example, every MUST item to buy.
%   comment   the same facts in words, the price where there is one, and the
%             free full-text link when one exists. Zotero imports it as a
%             child note; BibTeX and biblatex styles do not print it.
%   note      only what belongs in a printed reference (a paper number, a
%             reaffirmation year, "in Japanese"); most styles print it.
%
% In comment URLs a "~" is written %7E (the same address), because Zotero
% reads a bare "~" as a no-break space.
%
% Authors, titles, volumes and pages come from the DOI metadata (Crossref and
% DataCite, fetched 21 October 2026), corrected wherever the group checks or
% the document itself say otherwise; the sources with no DOI were entered from
% the checked citations. The year is the year of the issue or the edition, not
% the online-first date. Key format: <list id>-<first author><year>.
%
% Nothing here says a source has been read. Cite an entry only after someone
% has read the full text (READING_LIST.md, "How to use this list").

